            <ArticleTitle>Severe hip and knee pain in a man with chronic tophaceous gout.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1756-185X.2009.01385.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gout is a common rheumatologic condition with characteristic clinical presentations during the acute arthritis and chronic tophaceous stages. Because of this, there is a tendency to overlook rare but important conditions which are independent of, but can co-exist with gout. This case of severe hip and knee pain in a patient with tophaceous gout takes the reader on a problem-solving exercise which simulates the analytical processes and decisions made in the clinic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
